WEBVTT

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:31.295
we also had an issue
whereby most of our learning

00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:34.090
was characterized by rote memorization.

00:01:34.423 --> 00:01:37.093
On a typical day,
we showed up in a classroom,

00:01:37.135 --> 00:01:39.053
copied down notes that teachers gave us

00:01:39.095 --> 00:01:41.139
and were expected to go back home

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.349
[and] cram these in preparation for exams.

00:01:43.766 --> 00:01:46.811
And if I can be honest with you,
I did not enjoy this.

00:01:47.311 --> 00:01:51.524
We barely interacted with our teachers
and even amongst ourselves.

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:53.943
And even though as serious students,

00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:56.612
most of the time,
school seemed to be very boring.

00:01:56.946 --> 00:01:58.656
However, as I was growing up

00:01:58.698 --> 00:02:01.617
and as I took on the routine
of going to school in the morning